\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. GIVE heed, my heart, lift up thine eyes;
\par Who is it in yon manger lies?
\par Who is this child so young and fair?
\par The blessed Christ child lieth there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ah, Lord, who hast created all,
\par How hast Thou made Thee weak and small,
\par That Thou must choose thy infant bed
\par Where ass and ox but lately fed?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Were earth a thousand times as fair,
\par Beset with gold and jewels rare,
\par She yet were far too poor to be 
\par A narrow cradle, Lord, for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ah, dearest Jesus, holy child,
\par Make Thee a bed, soft, undefiled,
\par Within my heart, that it may be 
\par A quiet chamber kept for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. My heart for very joy doth leap,
\par My lips no more their silence keep;
\par I too must sing with joyful tongue
\par That sweetest ancient cradle-song:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Glory to God in highest heaven,
\par Who unto man His Son hath given;
\par While angels sing with pious mirth
\par A glad new year to all the earth.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

